<h1>🌎 Our Worlds</h1>
<p class="muted">One roof, separate rooms. Everything under this roof belongs to the <strong>Useful Appz</strong> studio — but each world is its own place, with its own page, its own rules, and its own door. Nothing bleeds from one world into another: the kids' worlds never point into the grown-up ones, and each brand lives on its own page.</p>

<div class="grid">
  <article class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
    <h2>🖋️ Tattoo Art Customs</h2>
    <p>Custom tattoo designs, a gallery of thousands of ready-to-ink pieces, working artists, and the studio's founding world. This site's home page is TAC's front door.</p>
    <p>What you do there: search thousands of original pieces across more than fifty styles, buy finished color artwork plus the clean linework a tattoo artist stencils from, or order a design drawn one-of-one at the custom desk. New designs land in the gallery every week, and every purchase pays the designer who drew the piece.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/">Enter Tattoo Art Customs</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
    <h2>🖍️ Little Inkers</h2>
    <p>The kids' coloring world — a free, kid-safe coloring book app with new packs every Monday. Walled garden: no accounts for kids, no tracking ads, no links out.</p>
    <p>What you do there: a child colors on screen, in the app — big bold pages drawn for small hands, with new packs to open every Monday. It is built to be handed over without a grown-up hovering: no accounts for kids, nothing to buy inside, and no link that leads out of the garden.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/little-inkers-android">Visit Little Inkers</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
    <h2>🌈 Poppy &amp; Ziggy</h2>
    <p>Our kids' cartoon from Little Inkers Studio — Poppy &amp; Ziggy color a page and it comes to life. New episode every Friday at 5 PM CT on YouTube.</p>
    <p>What you do there: watch the show. A full episode runs ten to twenty-three minutes, new every Friday at 5 PM CT on YouTube, with a short every day. Poppy &amp; Ziggy color a page, the page comes to life, and a little learning rides inside the game — the show's page carries the episode list and the cast.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/poppy-and-ziggy">Visit Poppy &amp; Ziggy</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
    <h2>🚐 HerbHaul <span class="badge">21+</span></h2>
    <p>Cannabis delivery, run by licensed retailers — HerbHaul is the ordering, dispatch, and proof-of-delivery platform they plug into. Adults only; demo stage, not live yet.</p>
    <p>Who it is for: licensed cannabis retailers who need ordering, dispatch, and proof of delivery without building their own platform. HerbHaul is in demo — the platform is being shown and tested with retailers, and no live orders run through it yet.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/herbhaul">Visit HerbHaul (21+)</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
    <h2>🧠 Chorvix</h2>
    <p>All your AIs, one team — one button, one conversation, every AI at the table. The flagship of the Useful Appz toolbox.</p>
    <p>Chorvix puts your AIs in one conversation instead of a dozen separate apps: you ask once, the seats talk to each other and build on each other's work, and you get one answer instead of five partial ones. It is in closed testing right now, and its own page says plainly which seats are actually configured — nothing is dressed up as live before it is.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/onemind">Visit Chorvix</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
    <h2>📚 The Library &amp; Dawnfold</h2>
    <p>The reading world: a massive library of books underneath a daily publication for grown-ups — the sections, the Sunday crossword, and the Everything Edition that carries it all.</p>
    <p>What you do there: read. The Library holds nearly 12,000 public-domain books, shelved by shelf and searchable, free to read. Dawnfold, the daily paper on top of the stacks, is one edition a day — front page, sections, and the Sunday crossword — written to be finished in one sitting, with a listen-aloud edition for the days your eyes are busy.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/apps">Find the Library on the apps page</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
    <h2>🧰 Useful Appz — the studio</h2>
    <p>The toolbox itself: every app the studio builds — the bars, the penny tools, the keeper and the doctor — in one lineup.</p>
    <p>Who it is for: independent developers and the people who use their apps. FillMyList fills the tester lists Google Play requires before an app may ship. Money Watch watches a developer's payout sources — the stores, PayPal, the affiliate networks, the bank — and reports the moment money lands. The Rolodex family keeps a business's links in one place — affiliate links, socials, storefronts — so a link lands once and stays current everywhere it is used. Email Keeper is a status board that shows whether each of the studio's mailboxes can still be read. The Odometer does the one job its name says.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/apps">Browse all Useful Appz apps</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
